A||||4||Wannabe||Re-applying GT sail panels||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||12-04-2000||10:24 AM||||Having successfully (an nesdlessly I found out later) removed the sail panels from my '87 GT and cleaned off all the adhesive, now I need to put them back on. Foam mounting tape doesn't seem to be up to the job, and silicone adhesive seems too extreme and irreversible. Any suggestions on how to re-attach these things?<p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||12-04-2000||11:02 AM||||I assume your trying to re-apply your ORIGINAL sail panels? If so, check with your local body shop supply store and find some 3M 3/8" wide double stick foam tape. That is what the factory used. Follow the instructions and make sure the both surfaces are clean and free of dirt, oil and grease.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||stsmithgt||12-04-2000||06:15 PM||||I found a role of that <B>3M super duty double stick foam tape </B>at Home Depot..Or was it Orchard Supply Hardware?  Anyway, it wasn't hard to find.  I found I didn't even need it.  The new panels came with the tape set up on them already. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-04-2000||06:44 PM||||Wannabe,<P>If you are having difficulty getting the foam tape to adhere, you could try an adhesion promoter.  Many 3M foam tapes require this substance to acheive the necessary bond strength.  Most adhesion promoter is essentially Nail Polish Remover.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000004||alpha||12-05-2000||03:51 PM|||| ....Most adhesion promoter is essentially Nail Polish Remover. <P>Which is essentially acetone.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
